ition/plannet-Endpoint"},{id:"Healthcare",description:"Plan Net Healthcare Service API covers data related to a healthcare service and services provided by an organization at a specific location. <br /> <br/>\n    The healthcare service resource typically describes services offered by an organization/practitioner at a location. The resource may be used to encompass a variety of services covering the entire healthcare spectrum, including promotion, prevention, diagnostics, hospital and ambulatory care, home care, long-term care, and other health-related and community services.",header:"Plan Net Healthcare Service",path:"/providerdirectory/healthcareService-api",url:"http://hl7.org/fhir/us/davinci-pdex-plan-net/StructureDefinition/plannet-HealthcareService"},{id:"Insurance",description:"An insurance plan provides health insurance coverage benefits that are offered under a network type. <br /> <br/>\n    The Insurance Plan API offers a health insurance list comprised of covered benefits (product), plan, administered by, coverage area, contact information, etc.",header:"Plan Net Insurance Plan",path:"/providerdirectory/insuranceplan-api",url:"http://hl7.org/fhir/us/davinci-pdex-plan-net/StructureDefinition/plannet-InsurancePlan"},{id:"Location",description:"Plan Net Location API provides detailed position/location information of the physical place that is associated with a patient, provider, or organization. Location may include private, public, mobile, or fixed. Location examples are buildings, wards, rooms, mobile clinics, vehicles, parking places, ambulances, etc. <br /> <br/>\n    Plan Net Location API return fields, including status (active, suspended, inactive), name, telecom, address, and managing organization (organization responsible).",header:"Plan Net Location",path:"/providerdirectory/location-api",url:"http://hl7.org/fhir/us/davinci-pdex-plan-net/StructureDefinition/plannet-Location"},{id:"Organization",description:"The organization resource describes a grouping of people or business entities relevant to the healthcare process. Organizations include hospitals, employers, insurance companies, physicians\u2019 offices, rehabilitation facilities, laboratories, etc.\n    <br /> <br/>\n    The Plan Net Organization API returns fields including Organization Identifier, Active (whether the organization is active), Type (type of organization), name, contact information, and address.",header:"Plan Net Organization",path:"/providerdirectory/organization-api",url:"http://hl7.org/fhir/us/davinci-pdex-plan-net/StructureDefinition/plannet-Organization"},{id:"OrganizationAffiliation",description:"Organization Affiliation defines a relation between two separate business entities. <br /> <br/>\n    Plan Net Organization Affiliation API returns fields including Organization, Participating organization, Period, active (organization affiliation record is in active use), Network and location.",header:"Plan Net Organization Affiliation",path:"/providerdirectory/organizationaffiliation-api",url:"http://hl7.org/fhir/us/davinci-pdex-plan-net/StructureDefinition/plannet-OrganizationAffiliation"},{id:"Practitioner",description:"The Plan Net Practitioner API provides information about a person formally involved in the healthcare process and healthcare-related services on behalf of a healthcare facility. Practitioners include, and are not limited to, physicians, nurses, pharmacists, therapists, technologists, and social workers.\n    <br /> <br/>\n    The Plan Net Practitioner API returns fields including Practitioner ID, NPI, name, address, and profile information.",header:"Plan Net Practitioner",path:"/providerdirectory/practitioner-api",url:"http://hl7.org/fhir/us/davinci-pdex-plan-net/StructureDefinition/plannet-Practitioner"},{id:"PractitionerRole",description:"The Plan Net Practitioner Role API covers data related to the type of services that a practitioner provides for an organization. The Plan Net Practitioner Role API returns fields including Practitioner, Organization (organization where the roles are available), code (role of the practitioner), specialty (specialty of the practitioner), location (the location(s) at which this practitioner provides care), and telecom (contact details).",header:"Plan Net Practitioner Role",path:"/providerdirectory/practitionerrole-api",url:"http://hl7.org/fhir/us/davinci-pdex-plan-net/StructureDefinition/plannet-PractitionerRole"},{id:"List",description:"The manager for resources of type CoveragePlan provides services to manage the collection of all the CoveragePlan instances.",header:"Coverage Plan",path:"/formulary/list-api",url:"https://hl7.org/fhir/us/davinci-drug-formulary/STU2.0.1"},{id:"Substance",description:"Medication(s) or substance(s) contained in the medication.",header:"Formulary Substance API",path:"/formulary/substance-api",url:"https://hl7.org/fhir/us/davinci-drug-formulary/STU2.0.1"},{id:"MedicationKnowledge",description:"The manager for resources of type FormularyDrug provides services to manage the collection of all the FormularyDrug instances.",header:"Formulary Drug",path:"/formulary/medicationknowledge-api",url:"https://hl7.org/fhir/us/davinci-drug-formulary/STU2.0.1"},{id:"AllergyIntolerance",description:"The Allergy Intolerance resource provides the clinical assessment of a patient\u2019s allergy or intolerance when exposed to a specific substance or class of substances, including information about the adverse reaction. <br/><br/>\n    The Allergy Intolerance API returns data fields including clinicalStatus , verificationStatus, code (code for an allergy or intolerance statement), patient, reactions (clinical symptoms and/or signs observed), and DateTime (when the allergy/intolerance was identified).",header:"Allergy Intolerance",path:"/patientAccess/allergyIntolerance-api",url:"http://hl7.org/fhir/us/core/StructureDefinition/us-core-allergyintolerance|6.1.0"},{id:"CarePlan",description:"The Care Plan API describes the intentions of how one or more practitioners plan to deliver care to a specific patient. Care plans are used in a variety of areas and scopes, ranging from encounter- or visit-specific to cross-visits. Care plans are used to group activities, goals, and/or practitioners to create context. Care plans are intended to be specific to the patient. It is possible for a planned activity to stand alone without a care plan, such as a scheduled appointment <br/><br/>\n    The Care Plan API covers data like ID, subject (patient), status, care plan, category (assess-plan), encounter, and period (time period plan covers).",header:"Care Plan",path:"/patientAccess/carePlan-api",url:"http://hl7.org/fhir/us/core/StructureDefinition/us-core-careplan|6.1.0"},{id:"CareTeam",description:"Care Team are the team people who participate in the delivery of care for a patient. <br/><br/>\n    The Care Team API covers data like ID, subject (patient), status, category (care team category), managing organization (organization responsible for the care team), etc.",header:"Care Team",path:"/patientAccess/careTeam-api",url:"http://hl7.org/fhir/us/core/StructureDefinition/us-core-careteam|6.1.0"},{id:"Condition",description:"The Condition resource is used to record details about a patient\u2019s problems, diagnoses, or other health matters that are concerning. It is common to capture conditions during the encounter or visit. <br/><br/>\n    The Condition API returns fields including category (assigned category to the condition), code (identification of the condition, problem, or diagnosis), clinical status (the clinical status of the condition), verification status (verification status to support clinical status of the condition), and subject (person who has the condition).",header:"Condition",path:"/patientAccess/condition-api",url:"http://hl7.org/fhir/us/core/StructureDefinition/us-core-condition-problems-health-concerns|6.1.0"},{id:"Coverage",description:"Data that reflect a payer\u2019s coverage that was effective as of the date of service or the date of admission of the claim. (*Based on the HL7 FHIR implementation guide found at https://build.fhir.org/ig/HL7/carin-bb/artifacts.html#3).",header:"C4BB Coverage",path:"/patientAccess/coverage-api",url:"http://hl7.org/fhir/us/carin-bb/StructureDefinition/C4BB-Coverage|2.0.0"},{id:"ExplanationOfBenefit",description:"The Explanation Of Benefit (EOB) resource combines key information from a claim, a claim response, and optional account information to inform a patient of the goods and services rendered by a provider and the settlement made under the patient's coverage in respect of that claim. <br/><br/>\n    The Explanation of Benefit resource may also be used as a resource for data exchange for bulk data analysis, as the resource encompasses claim, claim response, and coverage/eligibility information. <br/><br/>\n   Abstract parent profile that includes constraints that are common to the four specific ExplanationOfBenefit (EOB) profiles defined in this Implementation Guide. All EOB instances should be from one of the four concrete EOB profiles defined in this Implementation Guide: Inpatient, Outpatient, Pharmacy, and Professional/NonClinician. (*Based on the HL7 FHIR implementation guide found at https://build.fhir.org/ig/HL7/carin-bb/artifacts.html#3)",header:"C4BB Explanation Of Benefit",path:"/patientAccess/explanationOfBenefit-api",url:"http://hl7.org/fhir/us/carin-bb/StructureDefinition/C4BB-ExplanationOfBenefit-Inpatient-Institutional|2.0.0\nhttp://hl7.org/fhir/us/carin-bb/StructureDefinition/C4BB-ExplanationOfBenefit-Outpatient-Institutional|2.0.0\nhttp://hl7.org/fhir/us/carin-bb/StructureDefinition/C4BB-ExplanationOfBenefit-Pharmacy|2.0.0\nhttp://hl7.org/fhir/us/carin-bb/StructureDefinition/C4BB-ExplanationOfBenefit-Professional-NonClinician|2.0.0"},{id:"Goal",description:"A Goal resource is typically expressed as a desired outcome or health state to be achieved by a patient over a period or at a specific point in time. A Goal may address preventative health or mitigation of a diagnosis or problem. <br/><br/>\n    The Goal API returns data including lifecycle status (the state of the Goal), description (Goal description, e.g., control blood pressure, daily exercise, etc.), subject (patient), target (what should be done by when), and due date (date/duration the goal should be met).",header:"Goal",path:"/patientAccess/goal-api",url:"http://hl7.org/fhir/us/core/StructureDefinition/us-core-goal|6.1.0"},{id:"Immunization",description:"The Immunization API includes the view of current and historical administration of vaccinations to a patient in all healthcare settings. This API contains the functionality to query a patient\u2019s immunization history. <br/><br/>\n    Detailed administration records may be found in MedicationAdministration, while the Immunization API would represent the known vaccination history regardless of where the administration itself was done. <br/><br/>\n    The Immunization API returns fields including status, status reason, vaccine code, patient, encounter, occurrence, primary source, manufacturer, lot number, expiration date, dose quantity, performer, and note.",header:"Immunization",path:"/patientAccess/immunization-api",url:"http://hl7.org/fhir/us/core/StructureDefinition/us-core-immunization|6.1.0"},{id:"MedicationRequest",description:"The Medication Request API covers data related to all provider-prescribed, inpatient, outpatient-administered, and patient self-prescribed medication lists. <br/><br/>\n    The Medication Request API provides orders for all medications along with administration instructions for a patient in both the inpatient and outpatient settings (orders/prescriptions filled by a pharmacy and discharge medication orders).<br/><br/>\nThe Medication Request API returns fields including status, intent, reported medication, subject (patient), encounter, authored on (when the request was authored), requester, and dosage instruction (how medication should be taken).",header:"Medication Request",path:"/patientAccess/medicationRequest-api",url:"http://hl7.org/fhir/us/core/StructureDefinition/us-core-medicationrequest|6.1.0"},{id:"Observation",description:"Laboratory Result Observation API covers data related to patient lab results. <br/><br/>\n    API covers data like Status, Code (Lab report code), Subject(Patient), results and Effective Date and time.",header:"Observation",path:"/patientAccess/observation-api",url:"http://hl7.org/fhir/us/core/StructureDefinition/us-core-observation-lab|6.1.0"},{id:"Patient",description:"The Patient API provides general demographic information about a person receiving health care services from a specific organization. <br/><br/>\n    Patient API covers the patient's demographic data that is used to support financial, administrative, and logistic procedures. Patient records are created and maintained by the organization that is providing care.\n     <br/><br/>\n    The Patients API returns patients data, including family name, given name, address, date of birth, gender, and telecom.",header:"Patient",path:"/patientAccess/patient-api",url:"http://hl7.org/fhir/us/core/StructureDefinition/us-core-patient|6.1.0"},{id:"Procedure",description:"The Procedure API describes the request or order for a procedure or activity performed with or on a patient. This resource includes a wide range of requests, including surgery procedures, diagnostic procedures, therapies, patient care activities, referrals, and consults. This resource does NOT include medication, dietary, and appointment requests. <br/><br/>\n    The Procedure API returns fields including status, code, subject, encounter, and performed.",header:"Procedure",path:"/patientAccess/procedure-api",url:"http://hl7.org/fhir/us/core/StructureDefinition/us-core-procedure|6.1.0"},{id:"Group",description:"This Group End point explain to a provider how to use this endpoint to find the FHIR Group resource(s) containing their attributed members, which is required before initiating a bulk data export.  <br/><br/>\n    Groups conform to the PDexMemberMatchGroup profile and are identified by provider NPI.",header:"Group",path:"/provideracess/group-api",url:"https://build.fhir.org/ig/HL7/davinci-epdx/provider-access-api.html"},{id:"JobStatus",description:"This API explain that once a bulk export job completes, the 200 OK manifest from $exportstatus contains a list of NDJSON file URLs. <br/><br/>\n     Each URL must be downloaded individually using a valid Bearer token.",header:"Group Export",path:"/provideracess/group-export",url:"https://build.fhir.org/ig/HL7/davinci-epdx/provider-access-api.html"},{id:"DownloadFileAPI",description:"This API explain that once a bulk export job completes, the 200 OK manifest from $exportstatus contains a list of NDJSON file URLs. <br/><br/>\n     Each URL must be downloaded individually using a valid Bearer token.",header:"Group Export",path:"/provideracess/group-export",url:"https://build.fhir.org/ig/HL7/davinci-epdx/provider-access-api.html"},{id:"CrdServices",description:"The CRD Services API returns the list of CDS Hooks services supported by the payer for Coverage Requirements Discovery. <br/><br/>\n    Providers call this GET endpoint to discover available CRD hooks before invoking a specific service such as order-select.",header:"CRD Services",path:"/crd/cds-services",url:"http://hl7.org/fhir/us/davinci-crd/StructureDefinition/profile-coverage"},{id:"PriorAuthCheck",description:"The Prior Auth Check API lets providers verify, in real time, whether a proposed service requires prior authorization and what documentation the payer needs to make a determination. <br/><br/>\n    The endpoint accepts a JSON payload describing the patient, coverage, provider, and requested service, and returns the coverage determination along with any documentation requirements.",header:"CRD Prior Auth Check",path:"/crd/prior-auth-check",url:"http://hl7.org/fhir/us/davinci-crd/StructureDefinition/profile-coverage"},{id:"DTR",description:'Once CRD confirms that authorization is required, DTR (Documentation Templates and Rules) launches automatically \u2014 either as a SMART on FHIR application or natively inside the EHR. DTR retrieves a payer-specific questionnaire and uses CQL (Clinical Quality Language) logic to auto-populate fields with data already present in the patient\'s record. <br/><br/>\n    The provider only needs to complete the fields that cannot be automatically populated. This dramatically reduces the documentation burden and eliminates errors from manual data entry. <br/><br/>\n    DTR uses the $questionnaire-package FHIR operation to retrieve questionnaires and supports: <br/><br/>\n    <ul class="m-0! list-disc! pl-5! text-sm marker:text-(--moderatevioletcustom)">\n    <li class="list-item!">Standard questionnaires for straightforward, routine authorization scenarios</li>\n    <li class="list-item!">Adaptive questionnaires via $next-question \u2014 for complex clinical scenarios where the questions adapt dynamically based on previous answers</li>\n    </ul>',header:"DTR API",path:"/dtr",url:"http://hl7.org/fhir/us/davinci-dtr/"}],ze={healthcareid:{url:"https://api.aaneelconnect.com/cms/r4/providerdirectory/HealthcareService/{id}",codeurl:"https://api.aaneelconnect.com/cms/r4/providerdirectory/HealthcareService/id",languageurl:"http://hl7.org/fhir/us/davinci-pdex-plan-net/StructureDefinition/plannet-HealthcareService",path:[{id:1,label:"id",placeholder:"id",value:"",info:"Logical id of this artifact.",infobold:""}],header:[{id:2,label:"payer-id",placeholder:"payer-id",value:"",info:"Select Payer ID",infobold:""},{id:3,label:"Accept",placeholder:"application/json",value:"",info:"request HTTP header indicates which content types, expressed as request HTTP header indicates which content types, expressed as MIME types.",infobold:""}],queryParams:[{id:4,label:"payer-id",placeholder:"Enter Id",value:"",info:"Select Payer ID.",infobold:"",chain